From 10b26085de48e06ff64096354dcf722be6de98d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 04:15:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [DS4.1] rendezvous producers after empty waits and before
 buffer reuse

Base: candidate-38 on upstream 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 after the four local profiling fixes.

Rationale: a loop-entry rendezvous was insufficient. One full boot passed, but the repeat deadlocked in SwiGLU with producer warp 1 at an empty-barrier wait, the other producers at the next rendezvous, and consumers waiting for new copies. The elected copy can let consumers advance the empty barrier before a delayed non-copy producer observes its previous phase, even within an iteration. Rendezvous immediately after every producer empty wait, before any elected copy can reuse that buffer. SwiGLU has independent activation, gate and up waits; attention has separate K and V waits. Rendezvous after all three or both respectively, and after the single linear wait.

Quality: profiling off is unchanged. Profiling adds producer synchronization; ordinary performance must be measured separately. Preserve all copies and arithmetic, and refuse unexpected wait counts or non-standalone waits.

Tests: 20 CPU phase-pass cases pass, including after-wait/before-copy ordering and both dynamic attention waits and all three SwiGLU inputs. Hardware repeat boots are recorded in the deployment experiment. Upstream status: local experiment, not submitted.
